    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **66 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag: it's returned `true` when an owner's city already holds **40\u201349** owners (approaching the limit), while the hard 409 rejection at **50** is unchanged.\n\nChanges, following the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n2. **`rest/function/owner/AssignCapacityWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 counts the city's existing owners exactly as `CheckCityCapacity` does (case-insensitive, via `findAll()`), setting `capacityWarning = count \u2265 40 && count < 50`. Since the pipeline only reaches it after `CheckCityCapacity` passes, the count is at most 49.\n3. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignCapacityWarning` transactional step between `assignBulkSignupWarning` and `assignPossibleDuplicate`, so it counts persisted owners (excluding the new one) within the same write transaction.\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only boolean `capacityWarning` to the Owner response schema; the generated DTO field is auto-mapped by MapStruct (by name).\n5. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column so the persisted value survives the read-back (`hsqldb` is the test profile).\n\nThe relevant tests pass: `Cp54Tests` (the new warning behavior), `Cp18Tests` (hard 50 rejection unchanged), and `Cp22Tests` (bulk-signup warning regression), along with the rest of the suite.",
